answer-3d6d081e-5e34-5799-885e-d02bf5b30f41" "answer-239e272e-e941-51b1-88d1-658092cfdf99" "answer-0b94ed9c-f4fb-5037-a3fd-676575385f34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b420642-8b38-528a-b9fd-458b11392903" :answer/id #uuid "4b420642-8b38-528a-b9fd-458b11392903" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+12)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90614b3a-fb15-561e-801a-0578deafc573" :answer/id #uuid "90614b3a-fb15-561e-801a-0578deafc573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+24)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d6d081e-5e34-5799-885e-d02bf5b30f41" :answer/id #uuid "3d6d081e-5e34-5799-885e-d02bf5b30f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-12)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-239e272e-e941-51b1-88d1-658092cfdf99" :answer/id #uuid "239e272e-e941-51b1-88d1-658092cfdf99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-24)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b94ed9c-f4fb-5037-a3fd-676575385f34" :answer/id #uuid "0b94ed9c-f4fb-5037-a3fd-676575385f34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186272296 :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 5x+16\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $16$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{5}^{2}+16\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+5)^{2}-{5}^{2}+16\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+5)^{2}-9.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186271540 :answer-field/correct "answer-b69ae637-47df-5d0a-a406-5a5d5619d853" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53ee2aa7-49df-5b3a-8072-6c045e66c322" "answer-a61c1956-9aa0-5bda-b2b7-c15d6dd5eb67" "answer-8a5616f0-230f-5380-b162-0895d7287876" "answer-adae3f5a-4f4b